Plik 1.4.3

Hi, today we're releasing Plik 1.4.3, a security release !

The 1.4.2 Docker image is affected by several critical and high severity vulnerabilities
in its Alpine base (OpenSSL CVE-2026-31789, musl, zlib) and in its Go dependencies
(pgx CVE-2026-33815 / CVE-2026-33816, golang.org/x/net, golang.org/x/crypto, gRPC) and
standard library. The 1.4.3 image has no known fixable critical or high vulnerability,
upgrading is strongly recommended.

Here is the changelog:

New:
 - PKCE (S256) for all OAuth providers: Google, GitHub and OIDC (#730)
 - Display the basic auth credentials in the share card after an upload

Fix:
 - Charset-aware decoding in the file viewer (UTF-16 and other non UTF-8 text files)
 - CLI: identify OIDC users by their real ID in user/token commands
 - Self-host the Inter font instead of loading it from the Google Fonts CDN (@mouddane)
 - Helm: add the missing serviceaccount.yaml template (@rupertbenbrook)
 - Move the ? tooltips after the toggle switches in the upload sidebar

Misc:
 - Docker image based on Alpine 3.24

 Dependency upgrades:
 - Bump Go to 1.27.3 (crypto/x509 GO-2026-6809), golang.org/x/net to v0.60.0 and golang.org/x/crypto to v0.58.0
 - Bump github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 to v5.10.0 (fixes CVE-2026-33815, CVE-2026-33816)
 - Bump google.golang.org/grpc to v1.83.2
 - Bump gorm to v1.31.2, gorm postgres driver to v1.6.3, gormigrate to v2.1.7
 - Bump filippo.io/age to v1.3.2, golang.org/x/oauth2 to v0.37.0, mimetype to v1.4.16
 - Webapp security updates (Vue server renderer, DOMPurify, markdown-it, mermaid, lodash-es)
 - Bump GitHub Actions: checkout v7, setup-go v7, setup-node v7

Binaries will be built with Go 1.27.3

Faithfully,
The Plik team
